(RAG Document Assistant) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
/F2 14 Tf
(Project Report) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
T*
(A local, web-based document question-answering application built with HTML, JavaScript,) Tj
T*
(Python, and FastAPI.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(1. Executive Summary) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(This project implements a basic Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\)-style document) Tj
T*
(assistant. Users ask questions through a browser chat interface. A FastAPI backend reads a) Tj
T*
(local knowledge base, retrieves the most relevant paragraph using keyword overlap, and) Tj
T*
(returns that evidence to the user.) Tj
T*
T*
(The application demonstrates the full frontend-to-backend AI application flow: user input,) Tj
T*
(API communication, document retrieval, answer delivery, error handling, and a responsive) Tj
T*
(chat experience.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(2. Problem Statement) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(Teams often spend time searching policy documents, procedures, and operational notes for) Tj
T*
(simple answers. This project provides a lightweight assistant that can retrieve relevant) Tj
T*
(information from a maintained knowledge base.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(3. Objectives) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(- Build a browser-based chat interface for questions about internal documents.) Tj
T*
(- Create a FastAPI endpoint to receive and process questions.) Tj
T*
(- Retrieve the most relevant section from a local knowledge base.) Tj
T*
(- Return a clear fallback response when no relevant information is found.) Tj
T*
(- Add practical UI features such as Enter-to-send, a loading state, scrolling, and error) Tj
T*
(-   handling.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(4. Technology Stack) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(- Frontend: HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript.) Tj
T*
(- Backend: Python, FastAPI, Uvicorn, and Pydantic.) Tj
T*
(- Knowledge base: Plain-text file \(knowledge.txt\).) Tj
T*
(- Development environment: VS Code and Live Server.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(5. System Architecture) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(User -> index.html -> POST /ask -> FastAPI app.py -> knowledge.txt -> relevant paragraph ->) Tj
T*
(JSON response -> browser chat.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(6. Implementation Details) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
ET
