T*
/F2 13 Tf
(6.1 Frontend - index.html) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(The page contains a question input, Send button, and chat box. The sendMessage function) Tj
T*
(takes the question, displays it, and uses fetch to send a JSON POST request to) Tj
T*
(http://127.0.0.1:8000/ask. The returned answer is shown in the chat.) Tj
T*
T*
(The addMessage helper creates DOM elements using textContent and createTextNode rather than) Tj
T*
(inserting user text as HTML. This is safer because typed text is displayed as text, not) Tj
T*
(executable markup.) Tj
T*
T*
(- Enter key support sends the question without clicking Send.) Tj
T*
(- Thinking status gives the user feedback while a request is running.) Tj
T*
(- The input and button are disabled during the request to prevent duplicates.) Tj
T*
(- Automatic scrolling keeps the newest message visible.) Tj
T*
(- Error handling reports when the local backend is unavailable.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(6.2 Backend - app.py) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(FastAPI exposes a POST endpoint named /ask. Pydantic validates that every request contains a) Tj
T*
(question string. CORS middleware allows the browser page and local backend to communicate) Tj
T*
(while they run on different ports.) Tj
T*
T*
(The backend reads knowledge.txt and splits it into sections at blank lines. Each paragraph) Tj
T*
(is therefore treated as one retrieval chunk.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(6.3 Retrieval Logic) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(The words function converts text to lowercase and extracts alphabetic words of three or more) Tj
T*
(letters. For every paragraph, the application counts the words shared with the user's) Tj
T*
(question. The paragraph with the highest count is selected.) Tj
T*
T*
(For example, a question containing 'maintenance' matches the paragraph 'System maintenance) Tj
T*
(occurs every Sunday at midnight UTC.' If no words overlap, the app returns: I could not find) Tj
T*
(an answer in the knowledge base.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(7. RAG Explanation) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation. A production RAG system retrieves relevant) Tj
T*
(source text and passes it to a language model, which then writes a grounded answer. This) Tj
T*
(project implements the retrieval foundation and returns the retrieved evidence directly. It) Tj
T*
(does not yet use embeddings, a vector database, or an LLM.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(8. How to Run the Project) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(- Install dependencies: python -m pip install fastapi uvicorn) Tj
T*
(- Start the backend: python -m uvicorn app:app --reload) Tj
T*
ET
BT
