/F2 13 Tf
(9. Current Limitations) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(- Retrieval depends on exact keyword overlap; it does not understand semantic similarity.) Tj
T*
(- Only plain-text knowledge is supported.) Tj
T*
(- The system returns source text rather than an LLM-generated answer.) Tj
T*
(- The local CORS configuration allows all origins and should be restricted before) Tj
T*
(-   deployment.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(10. Future Enhancements) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(- Use embeddings and ChromaDB or FAISS for semantic search.) Tj
T*
(- Support PDF, CSV, and document uploads.) Tj
T*
(- Use an LLM to generate concise answers only from retrieved context.) Tj
T*
(- Add source citations, confidence scores, authentication, and a SQLite audit log.) Tj
T*
(- Extend the solution into an operations exception-resolution copilot for policies,) Tj
T*
(-   invoices, and SOPs.) Tj
T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf
(11. Conclusion) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
T*
(The RAG Document Assistant successfully proves an end-to-end AI application workflow. It) Tj
T*
(provides a strong foundation for a more advanced enterprise knowledge assistant because its) Tj
T*
(components are modular: the interface, API, retrieval logic, and knowledge base can each be) Tj
T*
(upgraded independently.) Tj
T*
T*
